# BEGIN open-source-core: attributes
# Owned by open-source-core (template/.gitattributes). Change it there, never in a copy: its tooling rewrites the copies.
# Text files are LF on every checkout: tests compare generated text with files in the repository
# byte for byte, and Git for Windows would otherwise check them out with CRLF. The app's own
# lines (a kind of file that is binary, say) go after this block, where they take precedence.
* text=auto eol=lf
# END open-source-core: attributes
# Manuscript's own: golden and round-trip tests compare the bytes of these.
*.docx binary
*.odt binary
*.rtf binary
*.pdf binary
*.wsmz binary
